        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-19T08:09:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In NPCX GPIO driver, we maintain a MIWU table to lookup the MIWU info of a GPIO pin.\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/bb5f16bd8b4b20182b2b426f0c0fd2f7953fe004/chip/npcx/gpio.c#46\nFor these GPIOs which do not support MIWU function should be declared as WUI_NONE.\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/bb5f16bd8b4b20182b2b426f0c0fd2f7953fe004/chip/npcx/gpio_chip-npcx7.h#172.\nBecause we borrow the GPIO macro to declare IOEX pins, they are included in the MIWU table as well. We have to define their MIWU info as WUI_NONE.",
      "parentUuid": "d48e673c_0828179a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 42,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 44,
        "endChar": 6
      },
